{"uid":"sn36.2","title":"Pleasure","reference":"Saṁyutta Nikāya 36.2","blocks":[{"kind":"prose","lines":["“Mendicants, there are these three feelings.","What three?"]},{"kind":"prose","lines":["Pleasant, painful, and neutral feeling.","These are the three feelings."]},{"kind":"verse","lines":["Whether it’s pleasant or painful,","as well as what’s neutral,","whatever there is that is felt","internally and externally:","having known, ‘this is suffering,","deceptive, breaking apart’,","seeing feelings vanish with every contact,","that’s how they become free of desire for them.”"]}]}
